---
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/chrome/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import SiteFooter from "@/components/chrome/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/chrome/SiteHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = "Calculator Methodology | Live Payout";
const description = "How Live Payout treats item price, shipping, commission, payment processing, cost of goods, and Whatnot fee-policy updates.";
const feeSource = "https://help.whatnot.com/hc/en-us/articles/4847069165965-Whatnot-seller-fees";
const breadcrumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Methodology" }];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath="/methodology/" {breadcrumbs}><SiteHeader /><main class="page shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Methodology" }]} /><p class="eyebrow">Methodology · 18 Aug 2026</p><h1>Show your work.</h1><p class="lede">Live Payout is designed so a seller can see where every dollar comes from and where it goes.</p><div class="content"><section><h2>What the calculator uses</h2><p>The US calculator separates item sale price, buyer-paid shipping, optional buyer-paid tax, seller-paid shipping, item cost, platform commission, and payment processing. That split mirrors the published fee components instead of hiding them inside one percentage.</p></section><section><h2>Published assumptions</h2><dl><div><dt>Other-category commission</dt><dd>8% of item sale price</dd></div><div><dt>Selected collectibles</dt><dd>8% up to $1,500; 0% above</dd></div><div><dt>Coins & Money</dt><dd>4% up to $1,500; 0% above</dd></div><div><dt>Pallets / Wholesale</dt><dd>4% of item sale price</dd></div><div><dt>Payment processing</dt><dd>2.9% of buyer order + $0.30</dd></div></dl><p>Source: <a href={feeSource} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Whatnot’s seller-fee policy ↗</a>. Whatnot describes the high-value and Pallets treatments as limited-time. These assumptions are displayed with a verification date.</p></section><section><h2>How payout and profit are calculated</h2><p>Buyer total equals item price plus entered buyer shipping and buyer-paid tax. Commission applies to the eligible item-price base. Processing applies to buyer total and the fixed charge is applied only when there is a paid order. Estimated payout equals item price minus commission, processing, and entered seller-paid shipping; estimated profit also subtracts the seller’s item cost.</p></section><section><h2>What it does not pretend to know</h2><p>Custom seller arrangements, promotions, taxes charged on seller fees, packaging, refunds, chargebacks, and currency conversion can change the economics. The calculator surfaces exclusions rather than silently inventing precision.</p></section><section><h2>Update policy</h2><p>When the source policy changes, the fee schedule is updated first, then the visible checked date and methodology copy are changed in the same release. Historical claims stay tied to their date.</p></section></div></main><SiteFooter /></BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page { max-width: 800px; padding-top: 76px; padding-bottom: 110px; } h1 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.8rem); line-height: .9; letter-spacing: -.08em; } .lede { max-width: 570px; margin: 28px 0 58px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.48; } .content { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } section { padding: 34px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } h2 { margin: 0 0 13px; font-size: 1.45rem; letter-spacing: -.04em; } p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; } a { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 750; text-underline-offset: 3px; } dl { margin: 20px 0; } dl div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 18px; padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } dl div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } dt { color: var(--muted); } dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 800; text-align: right; } @media (max-width: 640px) { .page { padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 70px; } }
</style>
